  "fixtureNotes": [
    "This fixture intentionally isolates a known base-allocation restriction from the unresolved later-purchase question.",
    "The base fixture remains numerically valid; changing Race to Lupus makes the existing Computer allocation mechanically invalid.",
    "Gnosis is deterministically rebased from Homid one to Lupus five.",
    "The invalid Computer allocation is preserved for explicit user repair rather than silently moved.",
    "Stable IDs, timestamps, fingerprints, and materialized ledger entries must be generated by the test builder.",
    "Chronicle owns patch application, persistence, invalidation history, transactions, and completion rollback.",
